== the variable, not its value ==
  changed after, read inside:  99
  changed inside, read after:  100
== a fresh counter every turn ==
  made in the loop: 1 2 3 
== naming two runs at once ==
  start at 100:       101 102 103 
  start moved to 200: 201 202 203 
== living past the call that made it ==
  5 through each:   15 and 6
== keeping an instance ==
  each its own:     10 and 100
  first raised:     12 and 100
== reaching a parent ==
  through the value: hush
  and its own:       HUSH
== a function with a name ==
  raised after by moved: 42
== declared in whatever order reads best ==
  4 even? true
  7 even? false
